                "quote": "let unreadable (name: string) = name.Contains ',' || name <> name.Trim() || name.Contains '\\n' || name.Contains '\\r'"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 62,
                "quote": "| Some m -> Error(InvalidInput $\"name of member {MemberId.value m.Id} cannot be written in the import format\")"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 31,
                "quote": "| Some loan -> $\"on loan until {Views.date loan.DueDate}\""
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "Branch lookup, copy listing and hold queues come from Tier 2 (Catalog.findBranch, Catalog.copiesAt, Holds.queueFor), and Tier 3 only formats them. Tier 3 also decides for itself that a member name is not exportable, which copies part of import-members' parsing rule (comma split plus trim). It reads the same way the import does, so it does not contradict it, but it is a domain-like validity rule in Tier 3 rather than a Tier 2 predicate that both import and export share. The loan-or-shelf status is derived in the Tier 3 report. That is projection and is tolerable. The extra export error is not in the requirement.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 37,
                "quote": "ports.Files.WriteLines path (\"copy,book,title,status\" :: rows)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All three new exports write through the existing Files port (ports.Files.WriteLines) and read state through ports.Store.Load. No clock, I/O or console is added in Tier 1/2. The CLI calls only Tier 3 Reports functions and renders the returned view, with no Persistence use and no Transition calls. The existing exportOverdue calls File.WriteAllLines directly, but it is untouched, so it does not count against this change set.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 60,
                "quote": "let unreadable (name: string) = name.Contains ',' || name <> name.Trim() ..."
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 66,
                "quote": "ports.Files.WriteLines path (\"member,type,name\" :: rows)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The member CSV format (the member,type,name header, comma separation, trimmed fields) is defined by import-members and restated in export-members, together with a hand-copied 'unreadable' predicate. The copies agree today, but nothing ties the export format to the import parser, so they could drift. Hold ordering and the DEC-005 queue come from Holds.queueFor, and branch handling comes from Catalog, so those facts are defined once.",
            "score": 1
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 193,
                "quote": "Catalog.addCopy { Id = CopyId copyId; Book = BookId bookId; Branch = branch.Id } library"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 34,
                "quote": "match Holds.queueFor copy.Book library with"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The rules for adding a copy (duplicate or unknown copy or book, DEC-011) are applied by Tier 2 Catalog.addCopy, and branch existence by Catalog.findBranch. Tier 3 only parses CSV lines, numbers them, and wraps errors, which is boundary translation. The held-copy status takes the hold count from Tier 2 Holds.queueFor and only formats it.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 181,
                "quote": "match ports.Files.ReadLines path with"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The file is read through the existing Files port. State is saved through the existing commit helper, which does all-or-nothing by folding on an immutable Library. No new effect appears in Tier 1/2, and the CLI only dispatches to the use case and renders the view.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 34,
                "quote": "| queue -> $\"on shelf ({queue.Length} holds waiting)\""
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The hold count comes from the single Holds.queueFor definition. The copy-addition rules are not restated, because Catalog.addCopy is reused. The import parsing mirrors importMembers' structure but contains no domain constants. The branch and book rules are defined once in Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          }
